„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙİSo they came up to Baal-perazim; and David smote them there. Then David said, God hath broken in upon mine enemies by mine hand like the breaking forth of waters: therefore they called the name of that place Baal-perazim.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙbAnd when they had left their gods there, David gave a commandment, and they were burned with fire.¦layout ªlast_verse…¤book§chapter«first_verseªlast_verse¦verses•„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙEAnd the Philistines yet again spread themselves abroad in the valley.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙœTherefore David enquired again of God; and God said unto him, Go not up after them; turn away from them, and come upon them over against the mulberry trees.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙÈAnd it shall be, when thou shalt hear a sound of going in the tops of the mulberry trees, that then thou shalt go out to battle: for God is gone forth before thee to smite the host of the Philistines.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙoDavid therefore did as God commanded him: and they smote the host of the Philistines from Gibeon even to Gazer.¦layout ªlast_verse„¥verse¯paragraph_startÂ¥lines‘‚¤textÙeAnd the fame of David went out into all lands; and the LORD brought the fear of him upon all nations.¦layout ªlast_verse